                <pb facs="0744" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg616"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 460.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Buck</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 10,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 19.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 22, of the 7th
                    ultimo, I have the pleasure to commend the terms of your note of the 4th ultimo
                    to the minister of state, in the case of the murdered American citizen, Owen
                    Young, as carrying out the instructions of the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
